d3a7721528d954b1c21b0750ba89bd2d6a39cb68 blob 11958
# Finite execution recipe — NOT RUN / NO CURRENT GO

Date: August 28, 2026. This file is a handoff contract, not a runnable new engine.

## Reuse and minimal future adapter

Reuse the exact coherent78 independent machinery pinned in BINDINGS.json:
- run-v2.mjs.data:50-86 inventory/diskUsage/tracked command receipts;
- :89-126 authenticated selected tree/tool reconstruction;
- :148-174 admitted module loader and one-ID child/result protocol;
- :236-270 selected build, full offline pack/install and physical move;
- loader.mjs.data (d0969da7...) and guard.mjs.data (aff310d8...) unchanged.

Do NOT launch that runner wholesale: it replays different C/R/H fixtures, a
structured-command mutant, old source review state and hardcoded component
witnesses. These are not authorized here. No old helper, source fixture, native
oracle, comparator, private runtime, arrays overlay or live HEAD may enter.

**Future owned path proposal:**
 tests/integration/priority-command-workflows-20260828/future-adapter.mjs.data
(not created). Root must grant an executor owner this path separately. Its minimal
contract is a case-data adapter plus orchestration parameterization of the above
qualified functions, not a new shell, registry implementation or comparator engine:

1. Accept exactly one packet ID, one layout and sealed admission/receipt paths;
   pass through the coordinator's existing parentBudget unchanged, use remaining
   counters/deadline, and never replenish it per layout/case. ParentBudget is a
   harness contract, NOT a fabricated Shell/public command option.
2. Replace fixed C/R/H selection with the sealed31 IDs; admit only this adapter,
   unchanged loader/guard and sealed fixture data. Do not add script interpreters
   to the harness. Shell.exec alone parses the literal script. No product command
   replacement, test-only register(), direct handler call or fake dispatch.
3. Use public imports from virtual-bash in installed/moved consumers, and the
   selected source-build package's public dist/index.js in source layout. New
   Shell({fs,cwd,env,limits}).use(agentCommands()) is the actual inspected API.
   The root barrel is transitively broad; future GO must admit its accepted module
   closure, not remove families to avoid loading them. No jq/engine behavior probe
   is planned. Explicit networkCommands({authorize,transport,limits}) is added only
   on the five curl rows, never silently by the aggregate plugin.
4. Build MemoryFileSystem, create /work and declared ancestors, write owned byte
   fixtures with mode0644, snapshot whole root, then install transparent VFS
   observation. C03 uses new ReadOnlyFileSystem(backing). C04's sole fault is a
   readStream iterator throwing the exact FsError descriptor before bytes. Neither
   wrapper invents provider capability/identity assertions. Setup/snapshot traffic
   has a separate role from observed product traffic.
5. Interpret declarative mock routes as HttpTransport infrastructure, never as
   command definitions. Before admitting cooperative host work, synchronously call
   request.registerCleanup with the same idempotent cleanup used by finally.
   Enforce exact URL/method/headers/body/authorization attempt and no extra routes.
   Each response iterator has owned chunks, finite pulls, return and dispose logs.
   Unexpected request/admission is a safety STOP, never a fallback to Node transport.
6. Supply fixture stdin as a bounded explicit iterator, or omit the option entirely.
   Never prebuffer opaque streams to fake cleanup. Preserve stdinIsDefault through
   transparent middleware. An observing middleware must await/return next() without
   changing command args, env, signal, sinks or shared Shell budget. Do not invent
   per-stage exec calls: real pipes must share one Shell.exec invocation. Find's
   aggregate child dispatch bypass may not be reported as a middleware invoke hit.
7. Capture stdoutBytes/stderrBytes, stage result observations and exact namespace.
   For throws, preserve actual reason references inside the child and emit only
   reference-comparison booleans; there is no result exit status. Assert full literal
   expected bytes/status and declared trace guards, not selected substrings.
8. Always await Shell.dispose, including failures. C05 tests two disposal calls
   sharing completion; it must not increment distinct Shell count. Retain observed
   operation/iterator/response/worker counts, listener ownership and pending gates.
   One created Shell and one completed underlying disposal per product row is the
   fixed rule. Opaque C07 settles by explicit fixture release after exec; root cleanup
   is never described as waiting for that opaque promise.

The adapter must also close G04: client.ts sets worker execArgv:[], so inheritance
of the parent loader/guard is false. Before GO, qualify a finite observer/guard for
Worker creation and entry/dependency bytes, using the existing loader/admission
protocol. Preserve actual Worker resourceLimits and product URL; do not replace
matching, force a TS fallback or change selected code. Any injected worker bootstrap
or execArgv is a disclosed harness semantic change requiring its own sealed review,
not an already-qualified transparent reuse. If the existing machinery cannot do
this within the granted adapter scope, HOLD and obtain a precise owner grant; do
not implement a second framework. Parent210 remains historical, not the expected
measured union for these rg cases. Record parent and worker loads separately.

## Authentication before any subject

Freeze this packet and future adapter before execution; reviewer uses literal
